<title>JAPAN: Mitsui Eng, Marubeni win Y17 bln power plant order.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Eng, Marubeni win Y17 bln power plant order.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Engineering &amp; Shipbuilding Co Ltd and trading house Marubeni Corp said on Thursday they had jointly won an order for a coal-fuelled power plant from Thailand's Hiang Seng Fibre Container Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The value of the turn-key order is about 17 billion yen, the two Japanese companies said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plant, to be completed in September 1999, will be capable of producing 150 megawatts of electricity, they said.</p>
</text>
